{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"","title":"Executive Summary","text":""},{"location":"#problem-statement","title":"Problem Statement","text":"<p>This project extends multi-view motion capture methodologies to both human subjects and arbitrary moving objects, with a particular research focus on the 3D reconstruction of Holstein dairy cows. The challenge is to achieve accurate, high-fidelity 3D reconstruction from calibrated multi-view camera rigs without predefined body models for the cows, overcoming issues related to occlusion, camera synchronization, and environment noise.</p>"},{"location":"#objectives","title":"Objectives","text":"<ul> <li>Implement a robust multi-view stereo (MVS) pipeline capable of reconstructing dynamic objects like dairy cows.</li> <li>Perform ablation studies (e.g., omitting specific cameras, altering contiguous/uniform camera subsets) to determine the minimal optimal rig setup.</li> <li>Integrate human pose estimation (MMPose, SMPL-X) and refine extremities (HaMeR hand refinement).</li> </ul>"},{"location":"#key-findings-results","title":"Key Findings &amp; Results","text":"<p>The ablation experiments on the Holstein dairy cow dataset (<code>cow-2026-07-29</code>) yielded insights into camera placement importance and reconstruction volume. Detailed plots and metric summaries for camera subset ablations and individual camera omissions can be found in the Experiments section.</p> <p>[!tip] Quick Link For instructions on setting up the environment, compiling dense MVS backends, and reproducing these results, see Setup &amp; Codebase.</p>"},{"location":"methodology/","title":"Methodology","text":""},{"location":"methodology/#theoretical-background","title":"Theoretical Background","text":"<p>The project's reconstruction methodology relies on classical (optimization-based) multi-view stereo (MVS), circumventing the need for predefined animal body models. The core pipeline is built as an independent fork of EasyMocap.</p>"},{"location":"methodology/#data-processing-object-reconstruction-pipeline","title":"Data Processing &amp; Object Reconstruction Pipeline","text":"<p>The reconstruction of moving objects (e.g., cows) follows a highly structured pipeline:</p> <ol> <li>Foreground Masking:     Segment Anything 3 (SAM3) is used to extract precise foreground masks of the subjects from the calibrated images.</li> <li>Sparse SfM (Structure from Motion):     COLMAP performs feature extraction, matching, RANSAC, and Bundle Adjustment (BA) to establish a sparse point cloud and verify camera poses.</li> <li>Dense MVS:     The dense reconstruction relies on several backends to ensure robustness, including COLMAP, ACMMP, DPE-MVS, and DVP-MVS. The fusion step operates with <code>--min_num_pixels=1</code>.</li> <li>Post-Filtering (Visual-Hull):     A visual-hull filter removes halo artifacts by eroding the SAM masks by a set dilation amount, preserving 3D points that project correctly into the cow masks across a minimum threshold of cameras (e.g., \\(\\ge\\) 9 out of 11 cameras).</li> </ol>"},{"location":"methodology/#experimental-design","title":"Experimental Design","text":"<p>The ablation studies (<code>cow-2026-07-29</code>) focus on evaluating the robustness of the dense MVS reconstruction. We systematically alter the available camera views during the Dense MVS phase: - K Contiguous/Uniform: Testing the impact of reducing the camera count \\(K\\) using uniformly spaced or contiguous camera clusters. - Omit Camera: Leave-one-out experiments to measure the unique contribution (importance) of each camera in the 11-camera rig.</p>"},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/","title":"Setup &amp; Codebase","text":""},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/#overview","title":"Overview","text":"<p>The primary codebase is located in the <code>motion-capture</code> repository, which operates independently from upstream EasyMocap. It contains the following core components:</p> <ul> <li><code>easymocap</code>: The core python package (loaders, SMPL fitting, camera I/O).</li> <li><code>apps/</code>: Applications for the pipeline.</li> <li><code>apps/calibration/</code>: Chessboard detection, intrinsics, and COLMAP BA.</li> <li><code>apps/demo/</code> &amp; <code>apps/preprocess/</code>: Human pose pipelines (2D keypoints \u2192 triangulation \u2192 SMPL-X).</li> <li><code>apps/handfix_hamer/</code>: HaMeR-based hand de-twisting.</li> <li><code>apps/reconstruction/</code>: Object (cow) MVS pipeline.</li> <li><code>scripts/</code>: SLURM launchers, demo production, and dataset preparation.</li> <li><code>config/</code>: Configuration yaml files for pipelines and visualization.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/#environment-hpc-setup","title":"Environment &amp; HPC Setup","text":"<p>This project was largely executed on the Digital Research Alliance of Canada (Alliance) cluster.  Key notes for reproducing on the cluster: - Python: Use <code>module load python</code> and standard virtual environments (<code>venv</code>) for python dependencies (Python 3.8+, PyTorch, OpenCV). - External Dependencies: You will need MMPose, COLMAP (built with CUDA), SMPL-X models, and Segment Anything 3 (SAM3). - Dense MVS Backends: Alternative dense backends (ACMMP, DPE-MVS, DVP-MVS) require specific Alliance build patches. - Slurm Gotchas: Beware of Slurm gotchas when requesting GPUs (e.g., specifying the exact memory and GPU type). Custom CUDA extensions might require careful Wheelhouse configurations.</p>"},{"location":"setup_and_codebase/#running-the-pipeline","title":"Running the Pipeline","text":"<p>Canonical commands for the cow reconstruction pipeline:</p> <p><pre><code># 1. Foreground masks\npython apps/reconstruction/preprocess_segment_sam3.py &lt;obj_path&gt; --frames 0:1426:5\n\n# 2. Per-frame MVS (SLURM array)\n./scripts/slurm/launch_4d_array.sh &lt;obj_path&gt; 0:1426:5\n\n# 3. Visual-hull post-filter\npython -m apps.reconstruction.tools.visual_hull_filter_pcd \\\n    &lt;fused.ply&gt; &lt;fused_filtered.ply&gt; \\\n    --sparse &lt;stage_a&gt;/work/frame_X/sparse/0 --masks &lt;dataset&gt;/masks \\\n    --frame &lt;frame_id&gt; --erode 8 --min-cams 9\n</code></pre> (Resource sizing: ~10\u201315 min per frame on an H100 MIG 3g.40gb node for the 11-camera 4K cow rig).</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/","title":"Ablation: K Contiguous","text":"<p>This section documents the ablation studies for this group.</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#overall-results-plot","title":"Overall Results Plot","text":""},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125","title":"ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125","text":"<ul> <li>Path: <code>cow-2026-07-29/ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125</code></li> <li>Objective: Test performance for configuration <code>ablation_k3_contiguous_frame125</code>.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#results-summary","title":"Results Summary","text":"<p>(Results to be populated from logs)</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940","title":"ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940","text":"<ul> <li>Path: <code>cow-2026-07-29/ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940</code></li> <li>Objective: Test performance for configuration <code>ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1940</code>.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#results-summary_1","title":"Results Summary","text":"<p>(Results to be populated from logs)</p>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_contiguous/#ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1980","title":"ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1980","text":"<ul> <li>Path: <code>cow-2026-07-29/ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1980</code></li> <li>Objective: Test performance for configuration <code>ablation_k3_contiguous_frame1980</code>.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"experiments/ablation_k_conti